msgctxt "adv_sign_in_browser"
msgid "Sign in with browser"
msgstr "ब्राउज़र से साइन इन करें"

#. Split rules sheet: the one-sentence explainer at the top, above the note on network clusters. A split rule sends the chosen sites directly from this device, outside the VPN; the sheet's Activity list shows how each connection was routed.
msgctxt "adv_split_rules_note"
msgid "Split rules let the sites you choose connect directly, outside the VPN, and the activity below shows how each connection was routed."
msgstr "स्प्लिट नियम आपकी चुनी हुई साइटों को VPN के बाहर सीधे कनेक्ट होने देते हैं, और नीचे दी गई गतिविधि दिखाती है कि हर कनेक्शन कैसे रूट किया गया।"

#. Windows sign-in screen, error line: a Google or Apple sign-in in the browser was turned back because this network has no such sign-in set up yet. Provider sign-in means signing in with a Google or Apple account, not a URnetwork provider. It points to signing in with email, or through the browser (Sign in with browser), instead.
msgctxt "adv_sso_not_configured"
msgid "Provider sign-in isn't available on this network yet — use email or browser sign-in"
msgstr "इस नेटवर्क पर Google या Apple से साइन इन अभी उपलब्ध नहीं है — ईमेल या ब्राउज़र से साइन इन करें"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode, the connection inspector and an Activity row's menu: the button on the confirmation after a press added a rule; it deletes the rule that was just added.
msgctxt "adv_undo"
msgid "Undo"
msgstr "पूर्ववत करें"

#. Connection inspector: exit value when the destination is not in the routing table.
msgctxt "adv_unknown_exit"
msgid "Not in the routing table"
msgstr "रूटिंग टेबल में नहीं है"

#. Connect page, Advanced Mode: the label of the verdict line (blocked, tunnelled, or bypassed the tunnel) in the connection details Copy details puts on the clipboard.
msgctxt "adv_verdict"
msgid "Verdict"
msgstr "निर्णय"

#. Connection inspector: verdict, the connection was blocked and no packets were sent.
msgctxt "adv_verdict_blocked"
msgid "Blocked — no packets sent"
msgstr "ब्लॉक किया गया — कोई पैकेट नहीं भेजा गया"

#. Connection inspector: verdict, the connection bypassed the tunnel and is not protected.
msgctxt "adv_verdict_local"
msgid "Bypassed the tunnel — not protected"
msgstr "टनल को बायपास किया — असुरक्षित"

#. Connection inspector: verdict, the connection went through the URnetwork tunnel.
msgctxt "adv_verdict_tunnelled"
msgid "Tunnelled through URnetwork"
msgstr "URnetwork के ज़रिए टनल किया गया"

#. Connection inspector: label of the via-exit row.
msgctxt "adv_via_exit"
msgid "Via exit"
msgstr "एग्ज़िट के ज़रिए"

#. Settings: heading of the advanced section.
msgctxt "advanced"
msgid "Advanced"
msgstr "उन्नत"

msgctxt "all_the_content_in_the_world_from_urnetwork"
msgid "All the content in the world from URnetwork"
msgstr "URnetwork से दुनिया भर की सामग्री"

#. Settings
msgctxt "allow_local_connections"
msgid "Allow local connections"
msgstr "स्थानीय कनेक्शन की अनुमति दें"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "allow_provider_cell_network_unlimited_plan"
msgid "You can also allow the provider to use cell network data, which works great if you have an unlimited plan."
msgstr "आप प्रदाता को सेल नेटवर्क डेटा का उपयोग करने की अनुमति भी दे सकते हैं, जो अनलिमिटेड प्लान होने पर बहुत अच्छा काम करता है।"

#. Call to action
msgctxt "allow_providing_cell"
msgid "Allow providing on cellular network"
msgstr "सेलुलर नेटवर्क पर प्रदान करने की अनुमति दें"

#. Text for a chip that indicates that the action is allowed.
msgctxt "allowed"
msgid "Allowed"
msgstr "अनुमत"

#. A label displaying the number of allowed and blocked actions.
