msgctxt "api_keys_empty"
msgid "You don't have any API keys."
msgstr "आपके पास कोई API कुंजी नहीं है।"

#. API keys screen (Account > API keys): a key's row, the line with the key's ID, shown so the user can use the ID with the API. {id} is the ID as is. Apple reads this English from the sessions_id entry ("ID %@", one catalog entry per English text), so this key is not tagged apple.
msgctxt "api_keys_id"
msgid "ID {}"
msgstr "ID {}"

#. API keys screen (Account > API keys): the explanation at the top of the screen. It must keep both points: a key lets the user's own tools and scripts use the account through the API, and anyone who has a key has full access to the account until the key is deleted.
msgctxt "api_keys_intro"
msgid "API keys let your own tools and scripts use your URnetwork account through the API. Anyone with a key has full access to your account until you delete it."
msgstr "API कुंजियों की मदद से आपके अपने टूल और स्क्रिप्ट API के ज़रिए आपके URnetwork खाते का उपयोग कर सकते हैं। जिसके पास भी कुंजी हो, उसे आपके खाते की पूरी पहुँच मिलती है, जब तक आप उसे डिलीट नहीं कर देते।"

#. API keys screen (Account > API keys): shown when the list of keys failed to load, above the retry button.
msgctxt "api_keys_load_failed"
msgid "Couldn't load your API keys. Try again."
msgstr "आपकी API कुंजियाँ लोड नहीं हो सकीं। पुनः प्रयास करें।"

#. API keys screen (Account > API keys): label of the name field in the form that creates a key. The name only helps the user tell keys apart ("home server"). Not plain "Name": apple has one catalog entry per English text, and name_label's "Name" reads as a person's name in several languages.
msgctxt "api_keys_name_label"
msgid "Key name"
msgstr "कुंजी का नाम"

#. API keys screen (Account > API keys): placeholder in the empty name field of the form that creates a key, suggesting a name that says where the key will be used.
msgctxt "api_keys_name_placeholder"
msgid "For example, home server"
msgstr "उदाहरण के लिए, होम सर्वर"

#. API keys screen (Account > API keys): the screen's title, and the label of the Account row that opens it. The screen lists the account's API keys, which let the user's own tools and scripts use the account through the API, and creates and deletes them.
msgctxt "api_keys_title"
msgid "API keys"
msgstr "API कुंजियाँ"

#. API keys screen (Account > API keys): the row title of a key that has no name (a key created through the API may have an empty name), and the {name} of api_keys_delete_confirm_body for such a key, where it appears between quotes.
msgctxt "api_keys_unnamed"
msgid "Unnamed key"
msgstr "बिना नाम की कुंजी"

